<Layout title="Privacy – WebP to PNG Converter" description="How the converter handles your images, temporary browser memory, downloads, and analytics. Images are processed locally without uploads.">
  <article class="article"><a class="breadcrumb" href="/">← Back to the converter</a><h1>Your files stay with you.</h1><p>This notice describes the behavior of this version of WebP to PNG Converter.</p><h2>Image processing</h2><p>Selected images are read, decoded, drawn to a canvas, and exported inside your browser. Images, original filenames, and local paths are not uploaded to a server or sent to a third-party image service.</p><p>Files and results are held temporarily in browser memory. Removing a file, clearing the queue, reloading, or closing the page discards the tool’s references to them. The tool does not use cookies, local storage, or IndexedDB to save images or conversion history.</p><h2>Downloads</h2><p>A download starts only when you choose a PNG or ZIP download action. Your browser controls the save location and may keep its own download history. Clearing this page does not delete a file you already downloaded.</p><h2>Website traffic and analytics</h2><p>{site.analytics ? <>This site sends limited usage events to <a href="https://plausible.io/data-policy">Plausible Analytics</a>: page visits, selected-file counts, conversions, download clicks, size and duration ranges, and predefined failure categories. The page address excludes query strings and fragments; referral information includes only the referring site’s origin. These events do not contain images, filenames, local paths, or raw errors. We do not load a session recorder or use cookies or browser storage for this analytics integration. Plausible receives normal connection information, including IP address and browser headers.</> : <>Production analytics is disabled on this build. No usage events are sent to an analytics service. The development server can print sanitized counts, ranges, and predefined failure categories in the browser console, without filenames, images, local paths, or raw errors.</>}</p><p>Loading the website still makes ordinary requests for HTML, scripts, styles, and public guide images. A hosting provider can receive normal request information such as an IP address and browser headers. That is separate from uploading your selected images.</p><h2>Future changes</h2><p>If analytics or hosting behavior changes, this notice must be updated to describe the services actually enabled. Contact information is listed on the <a href="/about/">About page</a> when available.</p></article>
</Layout>
